menu "AVB Bridge Configuration"

    config AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_MODE
        bool "Perf-test mode (skip PTP/AVB, blast AVTP frames out WiFi AP)"
        default n
        help
            Replaces the production bring-up with a pure data-plane test.
            Only NVS + esp_event + WiFi SoftAP come up; Ethernet, ptpd
            and the AVB stack are NOT started. A TX task loops
            esp_wifi_internal_tx with a pre-built AVTP-AAF frame so the
            path under measurement is P4 -> SDIO -> coprocessor ->
            802.11 -> STA. Counters are sampled by a 1 Hz stats task
            that logs pps and Mbps; the hot path itself does no
            logging or atomics. Pair with CONFIG_AVB_ENDPOINT_PERF_TEST_MODE
            on the C6 wireless endpoint to measure end-to-end.

    config AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_DEST_MAC
        string "Test destination MAC (six colon-separated hex octets)"
        default "91:e0:f0:00:fe:00"
        depends on AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_MODE
        help
            Destination MAC for the synthesised AVTP frames. Default is
            an AVTP multicast address. The endpoint perf-test mode's
            matching DEST_MAC must equal this for frames to be counted.

    config AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_STREAM_ID
        string "Test AVTP stream ID (eight colon-separated hex octets)"
        default "80:f1:b2:d2:ca:e0:00:01"
        depends on AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_MODE
        help
            8-byte stream_id placed at bytes [4..11] of the AVTP common
            header. Endpoint must match. Default uses the bridge's wired
            EMAC MAC suffix; any 64-bit value works.

    config AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_RX_MODE
        bool "Perf-test direction: RECEIVE (uplink) instead of transmit"
        default n
        depends on AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_MODE
        help
            Default (n) is the transmit role: blast AVTP frames down to
            associated STAs. Set y to invert the role — the SoftAP still
            comes up, but instead of transmitting, an RX hook on
            WIFI_IF_AP counts matching AVTP frames arriving from a STA.

            This exists to measure the uplink direction, which is not
            symmetric with downlink: downlink group-addressed frames are
            DTIM-buffered and never retried, while uplink frames carry
            Address 1 = BSSID (IEEE 802.11 Table 9-30) and so are ACKed
            and retried even when the MSDU is group addressed. Pair with
            CONFIG_AVB_ENDPOINT_PERF_TEST_TX_MODE on the endpoint.

    config AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_CHANNEL
        int "SoftAP channel for the perf-test AP"
        default 6
        range 1 13
        depends on AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_MODE
        help
            2.4 GHz channel the perf-test SoftAP beacons on. Sweeping
            this across 1 / 6 / 11 with everything else held constant
            separates "the link is contention-limited" from "the link
            is limited by SDIO and per-frame airtime" — the latter does
            not move with channel. The endpoint follows by SSID, so
            only this side needs rebuilding between runs.

    config AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_PAYLOAD_BYTES
        int "Payload bytes after the 24-byte AVTP header"
        default 192
        range 0 1400
        depends on AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_MODE
        help
            Total L2 frame length = 14 (Eth) + 4 (VLAN) + 24 (AVTP) +
            payload. Default 192 matches a Milan AAF stream at 48 kHz /
            8 ch / 24-bit-in-32 on Class A (6 samples * 8 ch * 4 B
            container). 96 = same format, 2 ch. 48 = Class B 48 kHz /
            2 ch / 16-bit.

    config AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_INTERVAL_US
        int "Inter-packet interval microseconds (0 = back-to-back)"
        default 0
        range 0 1000000
        depends on AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_MODE
        help
            Spacing between consecutive transmits. 0 means submit as
            fast as esp_wifi_internal_tx accepts (sustained rate is
            then the SDIO + 802.11 path's actual ceiling). 250 emulates
            Class B AAF cadence, 125 emulates Class A.

    config AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_DURATION_SEC
        int "Test duration seconds (0 = run forever)"
        default 10
        range 0 86400
        depends on AVB_BRIDGE_PERF_TEST_MODE
        help
            Counted from the moment the first STA associates and the TX
            loop actually begins. After expiry the TX task stops and
            prints a one-line summary; the SoftAP keeps running so the
            endpoint heartbeat continues to log final-second values.

endmenu
